M21 survives because no B3 block uses the link times of the timing contract, and U09's verdicts do not depend on them:
the mutant also passes the full U08-U09 with +U09_ALL (16x16, every subslot length up to SAFE, every region frame;
checks=4786633, run by hand on 8 Nov). With one-cycle hops the link uses move earlier but still never collide, and the
NI write port, not a link, sets TIGHT. Only the bypass datapath can show wrong link times, so B4's tests compare every
flit's cycle on each link and at the NI with tc_link and tc_eject (tracker: B4 exit check).
